    "chapter_label": "Respiration and transport in plants",
    "subtopic_id": "science/grade_07/ch_10/H013",
    "stem": "Kabir wants a fair test of whether warm or cold conditions change how fast water moves up a plant. He has two similar cut celery stalks, two glasses of the same red-coloured water, and can place one glass in a warm place and one in a cool place.\n\nAnswer both parts.",
    "item_type": "structured",
    "options": {},
    "statements": [],
    "parts": [
      {
        "id": "i",
        "text": "Which claim correctly designs that fair test?",
        "marks": 1,
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "text": "Use comparable stalks, the same coloured water, and change only temperature; judge the faster condition by which stalk shows the red colour higher sooner."
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "text": "Use a short stalk in warm water and a long stalk in cold water; whichever turns red at the top first shows the faster temperature condition."
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "text": "The stalk that turns red later transports water faster."
          },
          {
            "id": "D",
            "text": "A stalk without flowers cannot be used to test water transport speed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ii",
        "text": "Give one reason for your choice.",
        "marks": 1
      }
    ],
